// Typecheck the headless smoke scripts (issue #25).
//
// The smokes are the only end-to-end proof the transformed game boots, and they
// were the one body of code nothing checked: they are `.mjs`, so `pnpm -r build`
// (which is `tsc -p` per package plus `next build` / `vite build`) never looked at
// them, and vitest never imports them. A typo in a smoke surfaces as a confusing
// runtime failure during a release check — or worse, as a smoke that silently stops
// asserting what its name claims.
//
// The smokes span two packages (`@tspml/portal`, `@tspml/dev-harness`) and are
// the same kind of artifact, so one checker covers them all rather than two
// half-configs bolted onto packages whose own builds have a different remit. The
// globbed `include` below picks up new smokes automatically — don't count them here.
//
// `checkJs` on plain `.mjs` needs two things the scripts cannot declare themselves:
//   1. Node globals + `node:*` module types — hence `types: ["node"]`.
//   2. The bridge globals the smokes read INSIDE `page.evaluate()`. Those callbacks
//      run in the GAME's realm, where `window.__tspml` is installed at runtime, so
//      no static type exists. `smoke-globals.d.ts` declares them, deliberately as
//      `any` — see the rationale in that file.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "es2022",
    "module": "nodenext",
    "moduleResolution": "nodenext",
    "lib": ["es2022", "dom"],
    "types": ["node"],
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    // NOT strict, deliberately. When this was tried (at five smokes), `strict` produced 231
    // diagnostics, ~all of them `noImplicitAny` on inline callback params and
    // shape complaints about result objects that are built up field by field.
    // Annotating all of that would be a large diff that makes the smokes harder
    // to read in exchange for no defect caught.
    //
    // What non-strict `checkJs` still catches is exactly what a smoke gets wrong
    // in practice: a misspelled property on a typed value (`page.waitForTimeut`),
    // wrong arity on a Playwright call, a typo'd import, a `const` reassignment,
    // an await forgotten on a call whose result is then indexed. Those are the
    // failures that otherwise show up as a baffling runtime error thirty seconds
    // into a browser run.
    "strict": false
  },
  "include": [
    "smoke-globals.d.ts",
    "../../source/portal/scripts/**/*.mjs",
    "../../environments/dev-harness/scripts/**/*.mjs"
  ]
}
